ns (CCT) and aerospace aftermarket strength.\n- Further bolt-on M&A using still-strong equity currency.\n- Deleveraging to <2.0x during 2027 \u2192 upgrade optionality, resumed buybacks.\n\nRisks:\n- Integration execution (SPX FLOW is 3.5x larger than any prior ITT deal).\n- GAAP economics stay weak: net margin 5.8-6.4% in Q1-Q2 2026 due to\n  purchase accounting amortization \u2014 a multi-year GAAP drag on reported EPS\n  and ROE.\n- Industrial cycle rollover (ISM 55.6 historically near peaks; 30-40% base\n  rate of 40% drawdown for cyclical names within 3 years).\n- Leverage/covenant: 2.5x pro-forma; rising rates raise interest burden.\n- Aerospace aftermarket normalization (CCT organic was soft in parts of 2025\n  before kSARIA).\n- Tariffs/input costs (steel, copper) squeeze the 34.6% reported GM.\n- Impairment risk on ~$3-4B goodwill/intangibles if targets slip.\n\nPre-Mortem (5-year): The most likely failure path is (1) late-cycle order\npeak in 2026-27, (2) SPX FLOW integration costs exceeding synergies by 2:1,\n(3) GAAP EPS remaining below $6 for 3 years, (4) multiple compression to\n15x GAAP P/E \u2192 stock at $95-110. Early warning indicators: organic growth\n<3% for two quarters; FCF margin <11%; leverage >2.5x at end-2027;\nSPX order growth <0%.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2